            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Don1950"
            },
            "reviewBody": "They came out great but should have checked their progress at the 30 minute point but went the whole 45 and the could have moister for my taste. I know ovens vary on temps so this was my bad. Doing a couple of dozen for New Year’s Eve party. Quick and easy. No more grilled wings for me. Thanks for the recipe. Ow Bty, I put my wings oil and seasonings in a big bowl and rolled till well coated. Hate to waste a gal freezer bag and the seasonings stick to the bag as much as the do the chicken. My way was much faster and easier in my opinion.",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-30T18:56:41.522Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Vee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good. The wings were tender and moist. My husband is not a wing fan but even he agreed these were delicious. I increased the ingredients because I had about double the wings and mixed everything in a large bowl. I also added seasoning salt and baked on a cooling rack inside a baker sheet lined with aluminum foil. Will definitely make again.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-25T23:22:22.328Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RodneyL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These wings are fantastic. Followed another review and added 2tbsp of Franks wing sauce and 1 tsp of onion powder. I cut the olive oil to 2 tbsp since I’m adding more liquid with the wing sauce. Another trick is after baking put them under the broiler on low for about 3 minutes, turn wings and broil for another 2-3 mins. Crispy and perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-02T05:58:21.770Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Trisha"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect recipe! The wings came out tender and juicy. I flipped them every 20 minutes and brushed them with the rendered chicken fat and olive oil each time. After an hour, they were perfect. I used a berbere seasoning and served them with a yogurt sauce. Best roasted wig recipe I’ve tried so far.",
            "datePublished": "2019-01-28T00:02:41.650Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TabbiWytch"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved the combination of spices; even though I was out of garlic, I just used extra garlic powder and it worked just fine. I was very happy with how it turned out. I had to do the spices and oil in 2 batches. I did bake it for 15 minutes at 400 to help get the skin crispy, then 45 minutes at 375 - as the side I had went with the latter baking time and temp. So everything was done at the same time. This recipe is a keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2023-09-03T18:26:19.052Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GoldenWok8707"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Amazing recipe! Prepared as directed, except added to the marinade 2 tablespoons Franks Red Hot Sauce, and 1 teaspoon onion powder as another reviewer suggested. Marinaded for 6 hours, baked on Pam sprayed aluminum foil at 425 for 60 minutes. Delicious crisp wings, no fuss, no mess‼️",
            "datePublished": "2025-08-13T23:56:23.312Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jackiejo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this recipe! ❤️ I baked them at 425° for 20 minutes then broiled them for 6 minutes to get them crispy. I served them with Sweet Baby Ray's spread on top and grilled zucchini and carrots. Absolutely delicious 😋 😍",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-02T03:20:51.184Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JenM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tasty, but temp is WAY too low for crispy wings. 425 is a must. Flip every 20 minutes until crisp.",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-08T22:06:45.392Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BethR"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were pretty good and very moist. I thought I overcooked them and was afraid they would be dry. I was baking a corn casserole that needed 350 degrees, so I cooked them together at 365 degrees, adding 10 minutes to the wings. After they were finished and the casserole was out of the oven, I put the wings under the broiler, but they didn't get crispy, just a little more brown. An easy clean-up tip: line the pan with heavy duty foil and lightly coat with olive oil to keep the wings from sticking.",
            "datePublished": "2026-09-01T21:46:28.719Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
